{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92bafcb0acacb525b2532344dff1a8a5fb44a014.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(-3, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e2bf07828126b9fcb2c66f2b9aec62583db0305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(0, 7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc25931ef8baa460600605a93a5b46cf24c05748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(r, t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"20\" /> lie along a line. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/9/7196ff61f1feb011bd07d58d62e9c175a2ed91cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 4AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22ff7db3e755a8164f2344e0d3d84ea3a0fe93b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859f38daa3e2b3cf2f9e76407ccc93f36b92a7a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r + t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f35f5235a383688430f207a9e54f274a678ec28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is on the line, the function of the line must be of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1dd7bc03b1828985e64316cce1b2634f50d2f98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = mx + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is the slope of the line. We also have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/679704575d437f51af380423fd25f57c2e5541e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(-3) = -3m + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae6c10c6fa2e7a055e200432a2fbd5bbaf009318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 = -3m + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/6608edc7dcefae914e103fe18836ca04d4c59753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3m = 5 - 7 = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"153\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098264934ac94c339060ee4de62324f15ab25d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\frac{-2}{-3} = \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"107\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>This means that the function of the line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/392eaae3a494e0483a3ffc824c52862b9b2cfc70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\frac{2}{3}m + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6fc86a7d66ce478316f431d6e7d64553e336e5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = \\frac{2}{3}r + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distance_formula\" title=\"Distance formula\">distance formula</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b3174fcd1648f3e025e61074a74cbbe244401a25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = \\sqrt{3^{2} + 2^{2}} = \\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"182\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/9430d30720078da5b00086bf9e9b76d8e4bda744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 4 \\times \\sqrt{13} = \\sqrt{13 \\times 4^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"216\" height=\"21\" />. This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99cd3d707df45a3ba8c7c74c40538f3bbf8e4492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(r - 0)^{2} + (t - 7)^{2}} = \\sqrt{13 \\times 4^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"259\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a73198f5ab766c9177fa78d16b23a7e2a3a097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^{2} + (\\frac{2}{3}r + 7 - 7)^{2} = 13 \\times 4^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"227\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd55f23fcb1573c449d638fa5bad016564904c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^{2} + \\frac{4}{3^{2}} \\times r^{2} = 13 \\times 4^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"180\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/0/d90df332ebbf66d47c86e56f4b40e74d1dacb88a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{13}{3^{2}} \\times r^{2} = 13 \\times 4^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"163\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/e/9de116c20ed4337074b6471f1460a8b8906b9514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^{2} = \\frac{4^{2} \\times 13}{13} \\times 3^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"142\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/e/e8e6fb0583842b84e7a4fdc88ceaf7d57f46a7b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=(4 \\times 3)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/f/40f7e1b8190ffc7aba62cb9d022c1d20d4b0ceb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 4 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/9233c9f76a2b46c43f3e01373a366b33dc0deaf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Plugging this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/f/d5f03e9e373adb37fdaab39f7cfbdebdcc591d51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = \\frac{2}{3} \\times r + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/704975f3568d7e8a31d3eaf63cea32b75d10aeb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 12 + 7 = 8 + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"182\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53ed5cd8320d9c0ed2b5d6b3c4034eb36ac46619.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd0a64f7a6700f1ec4a1828a60d215e31c4ec0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r + t = \\boxed{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"93\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Pro